width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:9.8628em;\"><span style=\"top:-11.8679em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.0577em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">E13/3 = a</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.2628em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.0577em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">E12/2 = c</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.6526em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.0577em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">H/6 = N</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.0449em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.0577em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">E32 = a+</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:1.3451em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.0577em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:2.5451em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.0577em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">CLOSED</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:3.7451em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.0577em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">Heisenberg</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:4.9451em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.0577em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">grading -3, +3, 0</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:9.3628em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:19.2256em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-9.3628em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:11.8628em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:11.8628em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:11.8628em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:11.8628em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:11.8628em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-10.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:11.8628em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-14.5153em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:11.8628em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-18.1205em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:11.8628em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-21.7256em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:11.8628em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:9.3628em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[148]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{slot 8} & \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\0 & 0 & 0\\\\0 & 0 & 0\\end{pmatrix} & \\text{E13/3  =  a}\\\\\\hline\\text{slot 7} & \\begin{pmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\0 & 0 & 0\\\\0 & 0 & 0\\end{pmatrix} & \\text{E12/2  =  c}\\\\\\hline\\text{slot 5} & \\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac{1}{6} & 0 & 0\\\\0 & -\\frac{1}{6} & 0\\\\0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{pmatrix} & \\text{H/6    =  N}\\\\\\hline\\text{slot 3} & \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 0 & 0\\\\0 & 0 & 0\\\\0 & 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} & \\text{E32    =  a+}\\\\\\hline\\text{dim span} & 4 & \\\\\\hline\\text{dim span + all 16 commutators} & 4 & \\text{CLOSED}\\\\\\hline\\text{[a, a+] == c} & \\mathrm{True} & \\text{Heisenberg}\\\\\\hline\\text{[H, a], [H, a+], [H, c]} & \\left\\{\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True}\\right\\} & \\text{grading -3, +3, 0}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "973bf145-9d19-4b9d-a4a2-505573f957c3"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Conclusion — `adj (x) fund` gives *exactly* the same object\n\nThe localizing combinations of the 8 minimal-site-2 SoV covectors form a **4-dimensional** space,\nand its image on site 1 is **slots {3, 5, 7, 8}** — identical to `adj (x) adj`. Verified\nsymbolically in `h`, `θ[1]`, `θ[2]`, `z[1]`, `z[2]`, `z[3]`, not just at a sample point.\n\nSince the site-1 factor is the same adjoint GT basis, the identification is literally the same\nmatrix:\n\n```\n        [ -bb/6   aa/2   1/3  ]\n   Y =  [   0    -bb/6    0   ] ,   Det Y = bb^3/108 ,\n        [   0      cc    bb/3 ]     charpoly = (bb - 3t)(bb + 6t)^2/108\n```\n\nand the four directions again close into the **oscillator algebra**\n\n```\n   a = E13 (slot 8),  a+ = E32 (slot 3),  c = E12 (slot 7),  H = diag(-1,-1,2) (slot 5)\n   [a, a+] = c ,  c central ,  [H, a] = -3a ,  [H, a+] = +3a+ ,  [H, c] = 0\n```\n\nSo the object is rep-independent (at least across these two cases): it is a general element of the\nHeisenberg algebra plus its grading operator, sitting inside `gl(3)` — **not** `<e8| g` for any\n`g` in `GL(3)`, since `Y` is invertible whenever `bb != 0` while `<e8|` is rank-one nilpotent.\n\nSemisimple (hence `bb` times a rotated Cartan covector `<5|`) exactly on `cc = (3/4) aa bb`.\n\n### Pitfall\n\n`Solve[locEq == 0]` returns 4 branches and `Last` picks a **degenerate** one that only populates\nslots 7 and 8 — it looks like a 2-parameter answer. The generic branch, and the `NullSpace`\ncomputation above, both give the full 4-dimensional answer. Use the linear algebra, not `Last`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
